    "description": "Settings window: the sentence under the settingsWaveformsRiseFromTheBottom setting."
  },
  "settingsHelpWaveformsShowTheFrequencyStack": "A layer's waveform draws as three stacked waves — bass, middle and treble — instead of one. A loud passage is a solid block on a single wave whichever instrument is playing; the stack shows the kick apart from the hats, so a cut can be aimed at either. Turn it off for one plain wave.",
